WEBVTT

00:00.680 --> 00:04.310
Mother, when I'm really down on my luck,

00:04.310 --> 00:07.320
I have some great friends who support me and cheer me on.

00:07.940 --> 00:11.190
If I'm together with them, even without my brooch,

00:11.190 --> 00:14.990
I can bring myself to believe that one day I will meet you.

00:14.990 --> 00:16.910
Please wait for me, Mother!

00:26.420 --> 00:27.710
NAAJA

00:26.420 --> 00:27.710
Nadja,

00:27.840 --> 00:30.380
With your eyes

00:27.840 --> 00:30.380
Kimi no hitomi ni wa

00:30.380 --> 00:31.590
Nadja,

00:30.380 --> 00:31.590
NAAJA

00:31.630 --> 00:33.880
What do you see?

00:31.630 --> 00:33.880
Nani ga mieru

00:33.930 --> 00:36.800
Shining in the far distance,

00:33.930 --> 00:36.800
Haruka tooku hikaru

00:36.800 --> 00:39.180
The door to the future,

00:36.800 --> 00:39.180
Mirai no tobira

00:40.100 --> 00:43.560
That's what I'm searching for

00:40.100 --> 00:43.560
Sagashite iru

00:43.560 --> 00:50.780
Tomorrow's Nadja

00:51.480 --> 00:54.990
If everyone could meet with a smile

00:51.480 --> 00:54.990
Minna egao de aetara

00:55.070 --> 00:58.320
I'm sure there would be no more fighting

00:55.070 --> 00:58.320
Arasoi mo kitto nakunaru

00:58.370 --> 01:01.580
It could be so much more fun

00:58.370 --> 01:01.580
Konna ni mo tanoshi kunaru

01:01.620 --> 01:05.040
The world is wide, but it's still one

01:01.620 --> 01:05.040
Sekai wa hiroi kedo hitotsu ne

01:05.420 --> 01:08.710
I can't see the end of the journey

01:05.420 --> 01:08.710
Tabi no owari wa mienai

01:08.840 --> 01:12.170
God is the only one who could possibly know

01:08.840 --> 01:12.170
Kamisama ga tabun shitteru

01:12.340 --> 01:15.930
To the people who, someday, I will meet again

01:12.340 --> 01:15.930
Itsukamata deaeru hito tachi ni

01:15.970 --> 01:18.090
I will go waving

01:15.970 --> 01:18.090
Te wo furinagara

01:18.180 --> 01:24.850
Sometimes, there are days I feel blue,

01:18.180 --> 01:24.850
Toki ni wa BURUU ni naru hi mo aru kedo

01:24.890 --> 01:27.600
But I won't look back

01:24.890 --> 01:27.600
Ushiro mukanai

01:27.940 --> 01:32.900
Until the day my dream comes true

01:27.940 --> 01:32.900
Yume ga kanau hi made

01:33.190 --> 01:36.610
Nadja, Your smile

01:33.190 --> 01:36.610
NAAJA kimi no hohoemi wa

01:36.700 --> 01:40.030
Nadja, gives me courage

01:36.700 --> 01:40.030
NAAJA yuuki ni naru

01:40.070 --> 01:42.990
Under the blue sky,

01:40.070 --> 01:42.990
Aoi sora no shita de

01:43.120 --> 01:45.960
I will find the place

01:43.120 --> 01:45.960
Ashita no yukue

01:46.250 --> 01:50.170
where my future lies

01:46.250 --> 01:50.170
Mitsukeru kara

02:01.050 --> 02:01.640
There!

02:02.970 --> 02:03.640
There!

02:05.120 --> 02:06.330
﻿Yay!

02:14.760 --> 02:16.130
﻿Sorry to have kept you all waiting!

02:16.130 --> 02:18.670
﻿Presenting the miraculous dancing princess, Nadja!

02:28.890 --> 02:31.020
﻿Please. Stop the carriage.

02:33.900 --> 02:36.480
﻿My. What a lively dance.

02:36.490 --> 02:37.820
﻿Milady.

02:38.530 --> 02:43.620
﻿Ladies need not take notice of a dance from a mere traveling troupe.

02:43.620 --> 02:47.450
﻿Hasn't Duke Preminger always told you so?

02:48.080 --> 02:51.920
﻿Johanna, I'm now The lady of the Waltmüller house.

02:51.920 --> 02:57.420
﻿Because Father was with me last time, I was unable to see it.

02:57.420 --> 02:59.010
﻿Where's the harm in watching a little bit?

02:59.380 --> 03:02.640
﻿But! The wind has gotten colder as of late...

03:02.640 --> 03:05.970
﻿...if you were to catch a cold, I would be held responsible!

03:08.270 --> 03:10.730
﻿Really... you're such a worrywart.

03:11.480 --> 03:13.060
﻿All right.

03:13.060 --> 03:14.400
﻿Please carry on.

03:30.940 --> 03:35.940
The Wind's Trick, the Irony of Fate

03:37.630 --> 03:39.710
﻿We earned quite a bit today, didn't we?

03:39.720 --> 03:41.420
﻿Can we go to Vienna with this much?

03:41.430 --> 03:43.220
﻿Yeah. If we have this much...

03:43.590 --> 03:44.470
﻿Right?

03:44.800 --> 03:45.850
﻿All right!

03:45.850 --> 03:49.470
﻿How about we perform one more show tomorrow morning, then set off?

03:49.470 --> 03:50.520
﻿Really?!

03:50.520 --> 03:51.730
﻿Isn't that great?

03:51.730 --> 03:54.150
﻿Yeah! Thank you so much, everyone!

03:54.150 --> 03:57.860
﻿One person's happiness is the same as everyone's happiness in our troupe.

03:58.230 --> 03:58.980
﻿Yeah!

04:02.570 --> 04:06.950
﻿My brooch was taken from me, but... I still have the diary and dress.

04:06.950 --> 04:08.280
﻿I'm definitely not going to give up!

04:08.950 --> 04:12.410
﻿I'm sure that if I go to Vienna. I'll be able to learn something about Mother!

04:56.040 --> 04:57.920
﻿We should be able to leave by dusk, right?

04:58.290 --> 04:59.420
﻿Yeah.

04:59.710 --> 05:02.380
﻿In that ease, why don't I take care of some slipping before then.

05:02.590 --> 05:04.340
﻿Ah! Let me go with you too!

05:04.340 --> 05:05.590
﻿Me too!
Me too!

05:09.100 --> 05:10.430
﻿What are you going to buy first?

05:10.470 --> 05:11.560
﻿Let's see...

05:11.560 --> 05:12.520
﻿That candy!

05:13.180 --> 05:14.980
﻿Save that for later!

05:19.730 --> 05:21.070
﻿Wait!

05:22.190 --> 05:24.240
﻿Huh? Where did Nadja go?

05:26.030 --> 05:27.950
Off to chase after the wind.

05:29.530 --> 05:33.370
﻿She'll be fine on her own. Why don't we get to shopping then?

05:33.370 --> 05:34.870
Okay...

05:46.340 --> 05:47.420
﻿What a lovely woman...

05:48.640 --> 05:51.430
﻿But... have I met her somewhere be for...?

05:52.720 --> 05:54.470
﻿What an adorable girl.

05:55.390 --> 05:58.100
﻿But... have I met her somewhere before...

05:59.020 --> 06:01.190
﻿Ah! Thank you very much!

06:01.650 --> 06:03.360
﻿What a little prankster the wind is.

06:03.360 --> 06:05.940
﻿Sending your hat flying like that.

06:12.200 --> 06:14.660
﻿Welcome! What flower would you be interested in today?

06:15.540 --> 06:17.040
﻿Shh! Keep your voice low.

06:18.710 --> 06:20.230
It smells ﻿nice over here...

06:20.230 --> 06:22.110
It's kind of nostalgic...

06:22.110 --> 06:24.550
Is it the roses?

06:24.550 --> 06:26.260
No... it's not...

06:26.260 --> 06:27.670
﻿It's her.

06:30.800 --> 06:32.140
﻿Huh?

06:32.680 --> 06:34.100
﻿Has the carriage passed by?

06:36.450 --> 06:37.330
Yes.

06:38.270 --> 06:39.020
﻿I see.

06:39.440 --> 06:42.520
﻿Hey! Are you going to buy some flowers or not?

06:44.610 --> 06:47.690
﻿Then, um... two of those pink roses, please.

06:51.740 --> 06:56.160
﻿U-Um... miss, don't tell me... you're being chased down?

06:56.160 --> 07:01.960
﻿That's right. In the carriage that just passed by, is a terrible person trying to catch me.

07:03.630 --> 07:05.130
﻿Just kidding!

07:05.130 --> 07:07.380
﻿What? You scared me for a minute there.

07:07.380 --> 07:08.760
﻿I'm sorry.

07:08.760 --> 07:12.470
﻿But there's someone I have a difficult time with in that carriage.

07:12.470 --> 07:13.680
﻿Someone you have a difficult time with?

07:14.390 --> 07:19.180
﻿Even though I'm on vacation all the way in Rome it s always no to this and no to that.

07:19.180 --> 07:21.520
That's why I ran off on my own.

07:23.360 --> 07:26.980
﻿I decided that today, I'm going to do what I want to do.

07:26.980 --> 07:31.200
﻿Oh, I know! Would you join me for the day?

07:31.200 --> 07:33.160
﻿It would just be so dull by myself.

07:34.490 --> 07:36.530
H﻿ow about it? It's fine, right?

07:38.700 --> 07:39.950
﻿What should I do...

07:39.960 --> 07:42.290
﻿Granny and the others might be looking for me...

07:42.830 --> 07:45.290
﻿And today's supposed to be the day we leave for Vienna.

07:46.340 --> 07:48.750
﻿I guess it was presumptuous of me to think you'd agree...

07:49.130 --> 07:50.760
No, ﻿not at all! Of course not!

07:52.430 --> 07:54.260
﻿I was asking too much. Forgive me.

07:54.260 --> 07:55.220
﻿Have a good day.

08:03.400 --> 08:04.810
﻿Why...?

08:04.810 --> 08:09.190
﻿I want to be with this lady a little longer, who has such a nostalgic scent about her...

08:17.410 --> 08:20.660
﻿Miss! As long as it's before dusk, I'm free!

08:21.250 --> 08:22.710
﻿That's the way it has to be!

08:23.420 --> 08:26.130
﻿Is it really okay to leave Nadja be?

08:26.130 --> 08:28.880
﻿She might have gotten lost.

08:28.880 --> 08:31.460
﻿She'll be fine, she'll be fine!

08:32.970 --> 08:35.550
﻿Milady... where have you run off to?

08:39.100 --> 08:40.640
Caldar... roste?

08:40.970 --> 08:44.230
﻿Caldarroste. It's Italian for roasted chestnuts.

08:44.230 --> 08:47.310
﻿Ah! So that's what you meant!

08:48.110 --> 08:49.650
﻿They're so delicious, aren't they?

08:50.030 --> 08:52.900
﻿So satisfying and just a little sweet!
So satisfying and just a little sweet!

08:52.900 --> 08:53.570
﻿Oh!

08:53.570 --> 08:55.530
﻿We said the same thing!

09:00.160 --> 09:06.710
﻿When I was last here with my husband, there was this delectable roasted chestnut stall...

09:07.630 --> 09:11.710
﻿But, I can't remember where it was at all.

09:11.710 --> 09:15.920
﻿And since I was coming back to Rome, I was looking forward to eating them again...

09:15.930 --> 09:20.260
﻿Then why don't we go around to the same places you went with your husband?

09:20.260 --> 09:21.220
We ﻿might just find it!

09:21.220 --> 09:24.100
﻿Yes... yes, you're right!

09:24.140 --> 09:29.940
﻿Let's see... before, we went from the Roman Colosseum towards Tiber Island...

09:29.940 --> 09:32.440
﻿The Colosseum, right? Let's go!

09:32.690 --> 09:37.860
﻿My, my... If you don't pace yourself, you'll be exhausted before you reach the end.

09:41.030 --> 09:43.450
﻿What? Aunt Colette's gone missing?

09:43.450 --> 09:49.120
﻿When we were admiring the chapel in the Basilica Santa Maria sopra Minerva...

09:49.130 --> 09:51.670
﻿...she told me she was just going to take a look at the gardens...

09:51.670 --> 09:53.670
﻿..and handed this to me.

09:53.670 --> 09:55.420
﻿Since then, I haven't seen her.

09:56.930 --> 10:01.220
﻿There's a place I truly must visit. Please don't worry."

10:04.140 --> 10:06.810
﻿Despite how Aunt Colette looks, she's very a levelheaded woman.

10:06.810 --> 10:10.020
﻿What's more, Count Savelli's charity party is tomorrow.

10:10.020 --> 10:12.730
﻿Why don't you let her do what she wants today?

10:12.730 --> 10:14.320
﻿You must be joking!

10:15.860 --> 10:21.740
﻿If anything were to happen to her, what am I to say to milord and Duke Preminger?

10:22.120 --> 10:27.160
﻿If you were always this loud around me, even I'd want to run away...

10:27.910 --> 10:29.920
﻿W-What did you just say?!

10:30.290 --> 10:31.080
﻿Oh, nothing.

10:31.080 --> 10:34.210
﻿Lord Oscar, I never knew you could be such a cold man.

10:34.210 --> 10:37.380
﻿Very well, then! I shall go look for her myself!

10:38.590 --> 10:43.140
﻿But how will someone of my age be able to get around?

10:43.140 --> 10:45.600
﻿Oh, Milady!

10:48.140 --> 10:49.310
﻿Johanna!

10:55.610 --> 10:57.860
﻿It looks like it wasn't here...

10:57.860 --> 11:00.400
﻿After this, we went to the Roman Forum...

11:00.410 --> 11:02.870
﻿Ah, I've actually been there once before myself!

11:02.870 --> 11:04.990
﻿lt was so lovely there.

11:04.990 --> 11:10.250
﻿When I stood in there, it seemed like Caesar and Cleopatra were right in front of me.

11:10.790 --> 11:13.670
﻿Me too! I saw them too!

11:13.670 --> 11:15.090
﻿Really?

11:15.090 --> 11:16.090
﻿Yes!

11:16.380 --> 11:18.960
﻿Ah! It's the Mouth of Truth!

11:22.340 --> 11:25.720
﻿Ahh! I can't get my hand loose!

11:28.390 --> 11:30.100
﻿We're both kind of...

11:30.100 --> 11:31.350
﻿...alike, huh?

11:35.980 --> 11:40.570
﻿When I see this lady smiling, it kind of makes me feel all happy inside.

11:40.570 --> 11:42.450
﻿And I wish I could be with her forever.

12:04.550 --> 12:06.800
﻿Nadja still hasn't come back...

12:06.800 --> 12:09.060
﻿Don't worry.

12:09.060 --> 12:11.480
﻿She'll be back by dusk.

12:12.230 --> 12:16.520
﻿Look over there. It's the Broken Bridge, Ponte Rotto.

12:18.150 --> 12:20.110
It re﻿ally is broken!

12:20.820 --> 12:23.030
﻿I wonder if no one will fix it...?

12:23.700 --> 12:27.200
﻿Apparently the Ponte Rotto's been there since before Christ.

12:27.200 --> 12:32.410
﻿I wonder if the Romans like the way it is, full of history like that?

12:33.210 --> 12:37.040
﻿But it might really crumble one day...

12:37.380 --> 12:43.170
﻿What you really consider precious will continue to live on in your heart,

12:43.170 --> 12:46.090
﻿even after they're gone.

12:46.550 --> 12:49.050
﻿Yeah... I kind of understand what you're saying.

12:49.510 --> 12:52.470
﻿Now then, there's a flea market up ahead.

12:52.480 --> 12:56.520
﻿The roasted chestnut stall might be there

12:58.610 --> 13:04.150
﻿I'm so happy you decided to come looking for her with me, Lora Oscar!

13:04.900 --> 13:07.820
﻿You were planning on forcing this on me from the start...

13:14.120 --> 13:16.870
﻿It doesn't look like they're selling any roasted chestnuts here...

13:16.870 --> 13:19.250
﻿Even though there's so many stalls here too.

13:19.630 --> 13:23.510
﻿Oh you, the mother and daughter over there, how about trying some delicious panini?

13:23.720 --> 13:24.920
﻿Mother...

13:24.920 --> 13:26.800
﻿...and daughter, he said?

13:32.100 --> 13:35.270
﻿It would be so great if my mother was a person like this.

13:36.390 --> 13:39.600
﻿If she were still alive, I bet she'd be just like this.

13:44.570 --> 13:45.740
﻿But...

13:45.820 --> 13:48.160
﻿..until we find the roasted chestnuts...

13:48.160 --> 13:49.660
﻿We'll just have to be a little more patient!

14:00.340 --> 14:01.880
Miss, over here!

14:11.350 --> 14:13.510
﻿It looks like the terrible person didn't notice us!

14:13.510 --> 14:15.270
We ﻿sure managed to escape safely, huh?

14:16.910 --> 14:25.420
Let's climb up, let's climb up to that mountain blowing flame out from its top.

14:25.920 --> 14:35.060
Because inside of it is hell's kettle. Let's take a peek inside. Let's take a peek inside.

14:35.060 --> 14:44.020
There's a mountain railway already installed, so anyone can climb up!

14:44.440 --> 14:53.580
The flowing smoke invites all of us up, all of us up.

14:53.580 --> 14:57.910
Lets go, let's go, up to that volcano.

14:57.910 --> 15:01.380
Let's go, let's go, to the top of that mountain.

15:01.380 --> 15:06.000
Funiculi, funicula, funiculi, funicula!

15:06.000 --> 15:09.680
Everyone can take a ride up! Funiculi, funicula!

15:10.180 --> 15:14.140
Let's go, let's go, up to that volcano.

15:14.140 --> 15:17.560
Let's go, let's go, to the top of that mountain.

15:16.410 --> 15:17.580
﻿This is...

15:17.560 --> 15:22.520
Funiculi, funicula, funiculi, funicula!

15:17.580 --> 15:19.120
﻿This might be the place!

15:22.520 --> 15:26.020
Everyone can take a ride up! Funiculi, funicula!

15:26.050 --> 15:30.300
﻿Ahh... this smell! There's no mistaking it!

15:34.140 --> 15:35.600
﻿How is it, Miss?

15:36.930 --> 15:39.430
This ﻿is it! This is the taste!

15:39.430 --> 15:40.730
﻿All right!

15:48.190 --> 15:51.740
I can't believe we really found it. It's all thanks to you.

15:51.740 --> 15:54.660
﻿Me? I didn't do anything...

15:54.660 --> 16:00.000
If you hadn't come with me, I'm sure I would've given up halfway.

16:08.420 --> 16:11.420
﻿My! You're certainly good at climbing trees.

16:11.970 --> 16:13.380
﻿Why don't you climb up too Miss?

16:13.760 --> 16:18.720
﻿What? Me? I couldn't! I've never climbed up one before.

16:18.720 --> 16:23.690
﻿It'll be fine. This tree isn't too tall and there are lots of bumps, so it's easy to climb.

16:24.310 --> 16:25.650
﻿I wonder...

16:28.900 --> 16:31.820
﻿First, put your right foot on that large bump sticking out down there...

16:32.360 --> 16:34.650
﻿And then put your left leg up here!

16:34.660 --> 16:37.030
﻿All right, but don't let go.

16:37.450 --> 16:38.830
Up you go...!

16:39.950 --> 16:41.750
﻿See? You could climb up!

16:42.710 --> 16:43.960
﻿You're right.

16:43.960 --> 16:46.500
﻿I'm sure if a certain someone saw me, they'd faint for sure.

16:46.500 --> 16:47.380
﻿Look down there.

16:49.880 --> 16:51.250
﻿My!

16:51.880 --> 16:53.920
﻿What a lovely view!

16:53.930 --> 16:57.220
﻿It looks like we could see the end of the world from up here!

16:57.220 --> 17:02.220
﻿Back when I was in an orphanage, I'd climb up the tree there everyday...

17:02.230 --> 17:06.230
﻿..and wonder just what kind of people were underneath the wide sky.

17:06.520 --> 17:08.690
﻿Oh... an orphanage?

17:08.690 --> 17:11.690
﻿Have your mother and father passed away?

17:11.690 --> 17:13.940
﻿Apparently my mother's still alive.

17:13.950 --> 17:16.200
﻿But I just can't seem to find her..

17:16.200 --> 17:18.780
﻿Don't worry. I'm sure you'll be able to find her.

17:18.780 --> 17:23.160
﻿There's no way that God wouldn't smile upon a wonderful girl like yourself.

17:23.160 --> 17:23.750
﻿Yeah!

17:24.290 --> 17:27.620
﻿That's what I believe too! That I'll definitely find her one day!

17:29.210 --> 17:31.670
﻿Oh no! It's almost dusk!

17:33.340 --> 17:34.710
﻿There!

17:35.630 --> 17:38.090
Oh my...! How do I get down...?

17:38.590 --> 17:41.390
﻿Miss, please wait! I'll help you down!

17:43.180 --> 17:43.970
﻿Be careful!

17:52.570 --> 17:55.070
﻿Miss! Miss! Are you all right?!

17:55.650 --> 18:00.030
﻿I'm so sorry! Because I made you climb up the tree...

18:05.000 --> 18:10.380
It was my first time climbing up a tree, but also my first time falling out of one too.

18:11.150 --> 18:12.440
Miss...

18:19.970 --> 18:24.430
Ah... I feel a little as if my mother's chest would be this warm too...

18:25.430 --> 18:28.560
Mother, I want to hurry and meet you!

18:31.690 --> 18:33.980
﻿Miss, I have to go...

18:34.360 --> 18:37.030
﻿Yes... I must be taking my leave as well.

18:38.320 --> 18:40.910
﻿Today was truly a fun day.

18:40.910 --> 18:42.160
﻿It was for me too.

18:45.950 --> 18:47.160
Goodbye...

18:47.620 --> 18:48.910
﻿Goodbye...

18:58.920 --> 19:00.050
﻿Well then...

19:06.930 --> 19:10.640
﻿I'm so sad... why am I this sad...?

19:11.190 --> 19:15.070
﻿Ah... As we break up like this, it's as though we'll never meet again...

19:16.530 --> 19:17.530
﻿Little girl!

19:17.530 --> 19:18.360
﻿Little girl!

19:19.700 --> 19:21.570
﻿What's your name?

19:22.200 --> 19:23.490
Milady!
Na--!

19:24.200 --> 19:25.830
﻿Milady!

19:26.540 --> 19:28.290
﻿It really is you, Milady!

19:28.790 --> 19:30.500
﻿Thank heavens!

19:30.500 --> 19:33.750
﻿See? Aunt Colette was just fine.

19:33.750 --> 19:36.000
﻿And you got into such a fuss, Johanna...

19:36.380 --> 19:41.260
﻿I just wanted you to try some of these.

19:41.260 --> 19:42.220
﻿Here you go. They're roasted chestnuts.

19:42.720 --> 19:44.430
﻿My! Just to get something like that...

19:44.640 --> 19:46.390
﻿Th-Thank you.

19:49.980 --> 19:50.930
﻿It's delicious!

19:50.940 --> 19:51.940
﻿Isn't it?

19:51.980 --> 19:57.020
﻿Oh, that reminds me! I did something incredible today. I climbed up this tree!

19:57.020 --> 19:58.940
﻿My goodness...!

19:58.940 --> 20:00.650
﻿Why would you do something so reckless?

20:01.240 --> 20:03.950
﻿fRnic^this adoraolc little girl, ypu see...

20:03.950 --> 20:05.410
﻿See? She's right over ther—

20:07.660 --> 20:08.740
﻿My...

20:09.660 --> 20:11.620
﻿She's left already.

20:12.620 --> 20:14.830
﻿She was so lively and adorable.

20:18.750 --> 20:22.630
﻿I have to hurry and go... hurry and go to where Mother is!

20:24.260 --> 20:27.300
﻿If only her brooch hadn't been stolen,

20:27.300 --> 20:32.930
﻿Colette may have realized that Nadja was indeed her daughter.

20:33.890 --> 20:37.020
﻿At times, fate can truly be cruel.

20:39.280 --> 20:42.240
﻿Where did Nadja run off to?

20:42.240 --> 20:43.490
﻿Hey!

20:45.200 --> 20:46.070
﻿Nadja?

20:47.660 --> 20:48.740
﻿It's Nadja!

20:51.540 --> 20:53.460
﻿I can't just stand still.

20:54.420 --> 20:57.880
﻿I'm going to go to Vienna and find a clue about Mother for sure!

21:01.360 --> 21:03.820
